Z||000005||Matthew_Fiero||12-07-2001||02:49 PM||||i replaced the "can" under the steering column and the turn signals are still really slow. Anything else i should look at or consider?||||reg||1
Z||000006||TSPalmer||12-07-2001||03:24 PM||||Have you noticed in change in the speed between idle and if you nudge the gas a bit?  Could be a drain on the alt when the headlights are on and you use the turn signals.  My alt went south on me in town one day and I could rev the engine and the gauges would move (sitting at idle the gas gauge would show empty and when I revved on the engine it come back up to where it should have been). Basically I was running on the battery.  So you may want to check your alternator out.<P>Good Luck,<P>Shawn<BR><P>------------------<BR>T.Shawn Palmer<BR>'85 SE 4cyl 5spd||||reg||5
Z||000007||MinnGreenGT||12-07-2001||04:03 PM||||Are all of your blubs working properly... I understand that can cause a slow/non-working flasher.<P>You can also buy an electronic flasher... mine ran about $12 and is guaranteed for twice the life of a normal flasher.  It blinks faster and with a slightly different tone.<P>------------------<BR>              <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/GreenGT6.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000008||NEPTUNE||12-07-2001||04:18 PM||||Sounds kinda like the alternator is on the way out. Have it checked just so youll know.||||reg||1
Z||000009||Matthew_Fiero||12-07-2001||04:34 PM||||Could i test the altinator by turning on the car and unplugging the battery and checking to see if the car stays on?||||reg||1
Z||000010||rogergarrison||12-07-2001||04:53 PM||||  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Matthew_Fiero:<BR><B>Could i test the altinator by turning on the car and unplugging the battery and checking to see if the car stays on?</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I dont recommend you test alt that way, you could get a spike and fry your ecm. best to just hook a voltmeter to it. should be 13.5-14.5 volts with lites on.<P>On turn sig, replace it with heavy duty one, only a dollar more and not affected by number of lites on.<P><p>[This message has been edited by rogergarrison (edited 12-07-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000011||JohnF||12-07-2001||06:19 PM||||You need to check you side marker lights..One of them being out will give you squirrley turn signal.  <P>If all those are well, take it to Canadian Tire.  They'll run a quick check of you charging system under an induced load and tell you quickly if it is the battery, alternator or someting else.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=1578096&a=12001112&p=56509969&Sequence=0"> ||||reg||12
Z||000012||DJWINNI||12-07-2001||06:50 PM||||Hi!<BR> My problem with my turn signal is that the lights just stay on, and do not flash. Is it the flasher? I've removed it, and wanted to change it, but here in France it is very hard to find one like this flasher.<BR> Thus, I just wanted to know if someone could send me or sell me a non-used or a used one because I'm searching one for weeks. Plase, if someone could help, just contact me, it would be great! Thanks a lot for your help!<BR>Have fun........<P>------------------<BR> <A HREF="http://pageperso.aol.fr/djwinnimic/djwinnifierosignature.jpg" TARGET=_blank>pageperso.aol.fr/djwinnimic/djwinnifierosignature.jpg</A> ||||reg||1
